- Promises and fetch API
- Per-URL caching and cache invalidation
- Idempotent fetch behavior in UI components

## Code Example

```javascript
function createCachedFetcher(url) {
  const cache = new Map();
  return {
    fetchJson: () => {
      if (cache.has(url)) return cache.get(url);
      const p = fetch(url).then(res => {
        if (!res.ok) throw new Error(res.statusText);
        return res.json();
      });
      cache.set(url, p);
      return p;
    },
    invalidate: () => cache.delete(url)
  };
}
```

